  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nPeriods of showers and storms through the weekend from the effects \nof daytime heating and occasional shortwaves moving through the \narea. Overall, the threat of severe appears to be low, but not \ncompletely out of the question, with at least modest instability and \nabove normal PWATs expected, with an isolated damaging wind threat, \nparticularly on Saturday with drier air in lower levels/DCAPE values \npotentially over 1000 J/Kg. Localized instances of flash flooding \nwill also be possible at times over the next few days, particularly \ndue to the rather light steering flow along with the above normal \nPWATs.\n\nThere may be a brief lull in convective activity on Sunday as some \nmodels are indicating weak high pressure taking hold, but activity \nlooks to ramp back up again Monday through the remainder of the \nextended, as broad troughing takes hold across the eastern U.S., \nwith multiple waves of convection moving into the area on \nnorthwesterly flow. Although its too early to say, some of these \ncould produce severe weather in the form of damaging winds.",
